{
  "_readme": [
    "Every fact the tutorial teaches about CareJioX is declared here, together with",
    "where it came from. `tools/check_contract.py` re-reads the addons and fails when a",
    "declaration no longer holds, naming the fixture entries and lesson content that",
    "quote it. This is the mechanism that keeps a JS-fixture practice clinic honest",
    "without an isolated tenant.",
    "",
    "When a check fails you have two correct responses, and one wrong one:",
    "  1. The product changed on purpose  -> update `expect` here, then practice-data.js,",
    "     then the `taughtIn` content listed on the entry.",
    "  2. The product changed by accident -> fix the product.",
    "  3. WRONG: relax the check. A green checker that proves nothing is worse than no",
    "     checker, because it buys false confidence in a tutorial people trust."
  ],
  "schemaVersion": "1.1.0",
  "repoRoot": "../..",
  "checks": [
    {
      "id": "urgency-terms",
      "why": "The whole worked case sums to 110. If any weight moves, every lesson step, coach calc-block and mission fact that quotes it becomes wrong at once.",
      "kind": "constants",
      "file": "addons/health_care_command/models/care_conversation.py",
      "within": "_compute_urgency_score",
      "expect": {
        "score += 40": {
          "means": "needs_reply",
          "count": 1
        },
        "score += 30": {
          "means": "booking within 24h",
          "count": 1
        },
        "score += 15": {
          "means": "unread>0 AND watch phrase — two separate terms",
          "count": 2
        },
        "score += 10": {
          "means": "unhandled missed call",
          "count": 1
        },
        "min(20,": {
          "means": "ageing cap",
          "count": 1
        }
      },
      "fixture": [
        "CASE.urgency",
        "CASE.urgencyTotal",
        "CASE.urgencyLater"
      ],
      "taughtIn": [
        "L1 step 4",
        "L1 step 5",
        "L1 quiz",
        "QA:urgency",
        "M1 step 1",
        "glossary:urgency"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "conversation-status",
      "why": "The lifecycle pipeline animation and the Junk? consequence both name these values.",
      "kind": "selection",
      "file": "addons/health_care_command/models/care_conversation.py",
      "expect": [
        "needs_reply",
        "waiting",
        "junk_suspect",
        "closed"
      ],
      "fixture": [
        "PRACTICE.conversations[].status",
        "STATUS_LABELS.conversation"
      ],
      "taughtIn": [
        "L1 step 7 (pipeline)",
        "QA:junk",
        "M1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "junk-side-effect",
      "why": "L1's morph and M1's recovery both claim that marking Junk? ALSO spams the linked lead. If that call is removed, the tutorial is teaching a consequence that no longer exists.",
      "kind": "contains",
      "file": "addons/health_care_command/models/care_conversation.py",
      "expect": [
        "action_mark_spam"
      ],
      "fixture": [],
      "taughtIn": [
